# RESOLVED 2026-08-10: KNN, Parallel, KNNFewShot, and Ensemble were previously excluded here.
# All four were actually constructed AND executed against the real installed dspy 3.1.3 this
# session (KNN via dspy:trainsetName/dspy:usesEmbedder/dspy:kValue on a "KNN"-kind Module;
# Parallel via dspy:hasParallelStep; Ensemble via the dedicated dspy:hasEnsembleMember property,
# since its real compile(programs) genuinely takes a list with no metric/target-Module concept;
# KNNFewShot via the normal dspy:optimizes shape plus dspy:kValue/dspy:trainsetName/
# dspy:usesEmbedder) with no bugs found. "Pipeline" and "MultiHop" are two new admitted Module
# kinds that aren't literal 1:1 dspy source classes -- they're this pack's own composition
# constructs (an ordered dspy:PipelineStep sequence with dspy:ArgBinding data-flow wiring; a
# fixed, parameterized retrieve-then-reason recipe) admitted because they render real,
# actually-executed dspy code (dspy.Retrieve wired into ChainOfThought/Predict steps), not
# because a single dspy class named "Pipeline"/"MultiHop" exists upstream -- included in the
# AdmittedKind set above for the drift guard's own bookkeeping, not cross-referenced against a
# dspyaud:DSPySourceClass entry the way every other admitted kind is.
